You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Scroll Mask Expand (`gsap-mask-expand`)

A small rounded window between two words grows to full screen as you scroll, pushing the words apart and zooming the photo out — curtains-open reveal.

## What it should do
Build a mask expand: 260vh section, sticky stage; image wrapper clipPath inset(38% 39% 38% 39% round 24px) → inset(0 round 0) and image scale 1.5→1 (power2.inOut), left/right words xPercent ∓140 + fade, caption rising at .7 — all in one timeline with scrollTrigger { start top top, end bottom bottom, scrub .6 }.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **gsap**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i gsap @gsap/react`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/gsap-mask-expand.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Words are a decorative duplicate (aria-hidden); real heading lives in children. Reduced motion shows the full image.
- **Performance:** clip-path + transforms in one scrubbed timeline.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

